  "notes": "A spatial dataflow pipeline: the program Map over (i, j) of Fold over k is laid out as wired units with no instruction loop. Two chained counters issue one (i, j) item per cycle; two scratchpad units rotate so that their fixed read ports show row i of A and column j of B; one compute unit multiplies N lanes and sums them in a registered binary tree; an output unit shifts each dot product into C, and the last one raises done. N*N dot products are in flight at once. Latency N*N + clog2(N) + 2 (20 at N = 4). The tree's register vector has 2*P*AccW bits (P = N rounded up to a power of two), more than 2^31 only at N = 1 with AccW >= 2^30.",
  "player": "quillwren",
